# ⚠️ These must reach Linux with LF endings, whatever the checkout they were edited in.
# A shell script with CRLF fails as `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`, and a systemd
# unit with CRLF is rejected about as unhelpfully — both only after being edited on a
# Windows working copy, where autocrlf would otherwise convert them on the way out.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.service  text eol=lf
